<Project>
  <!-- Imported automatically into any project with a PackageReference to
       GHIElectronics.Endpoint.Drivers.RaspberryPi.

       Pin constants are `const`, so the C# compiler inlines their values and
       the consumer's IL never names this assembly. Reachability analysis then
       sees an unused package: a trimmed or Native AOT publish (Ctrl+F5) drops
       the .dll outright, its [ModuleInitializer] never runs, no board
       registers, and every peripheral call throws "not supported on this
       board". Rooting the assembly keeps it in the output so the initializer
       runs.

       The JIT path (F5, endpoint-cli deploy) does not trim, and is handled in
       GHIElectronics.Endpoint.Core by BoardSupport loading this assembly by
       name. The two cover each other; neither covers both on its own. -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="GHIElectronics.Endpoint.Drivers.RaspberryPi" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
